Return your final response within \boxed{}. Find the probability that heads will appear an even number of times in an experiment where:

a) a fair coin is tossed $n$ times;

b) a coin with the probability of heads being $p$ ($0 < p < 1$) is tossed $n$ times.

Return your final response within \boxed{}. An unbiased six-sided die is numbered 1 to 6. The die is thrown twice and the two scores are added. Which of the following events has the highest probability of occurrence?
(A) The total score is a prime number;
(B) The total score is a multiple of 4;
(C) The total score is a perfect square;
(D) The total score is 7;
(E) The total score is a factor of 12.

Return your final response within \boxed{}. A die is rolled. Find the probability that:
a) an even number of points appears (event $A$);
b) a number of points that is a multiple of 3 appears (event $B$);
c) any number of points appears except 5 (event $C$).
